(271, 15, 'The standard length for most electrical conduits in the Philippines is 10 feet (3.05 meters).', 'true_false'),
(272, 15, 'Schedule 80 PVC has a thinner wall than Schedule 40 PVC.', 'true_false'),
(273, 15, 'EMT is often referred to as thin-wall conduit.', 'true_false'),
(274, 15, 'RSC and IMC generally share the same outside diameter, allowing them to use similar threaded fittings.', 'true_false'),
(275, 15, 'Set-screw and compression fittings are the primary ways to join PVC conduits.', 'true_false'),
(276, 15, 'RSC is typically identified by a red label or marking.', 'true_false'),
(277, 15, 'According to the PEC, PVC is the best choice for areas with high salt air concentration, such as coastal regions.', 'true_false'),
(278, 15, 'IMC uses a specialized steel alloy that allows it to be lighter than RSC while maintaining high strength.', 'true_false'),
(279, 15, 'EMT is recommended for use in locations where it will be subject to severe physical impact.', 'true_false'),
(280, 15, 'Solvent cement (chemical welding) is used to create waterproof joints in PVC conduit systems.', 'true_false'),
(281, 15, 'A hickey or hand bender is the standard tool used to bend heavy-wall RSC.', 'true_false'),
(282, 16, 'What is the maximum total number of degrees of bends allowed between pull points according to the PEC?', 'multiple_choice'),
(283, 16, 'When interpreting an electrical drawing, what does a dashed line typically represent?', 'multiple_choice'),
(284, 16, 'If you are using a 1/2 inch EMT bender, what is the standard Take-Up value for a 90-degree stub-up?', 'multiple_choice'),
(285, 16, 'Why is it critical to ream the ends of a conduit after cutting?', 'multiple_choice'),
(286, 16, 'What is the multiplier used to calculate the distance between marks for a 30-degree offset bend?', 'multiple_choice'),
(287, 16, 'According to PEC standards, conduit must generally be supported within how many meters of every outlet box or fitting?', 'multiple_choice'),
(288, 16, 'Which tool is used to ensure that a vertical conduit run is perfectly straight up and down?', 'multiple_choice'),
(289, 16, 'In an offset bend, what happens to the total length of the conduit run?', 'multiple_choice'),
(290, 16, 'Where would you find the specific conduit and wire sizes required for a project on an electrical plan?', 'multiple_choice'),
(291, 16, 'What is the result of a bend that is kinked or flattened?', 'multiple_choice');

